<h2 class="font-headline-md text-headline-md text-primary mb-4">Types of Soft Tissue Infections of the Face</h2>
</div>
<div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Cellulitis</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Diffuse bacterial infection spreading through skin layers and subcutaneous fat. Causes poorly defined redness, warmth, and swelling. Oral or IV antibiotics are the mainstay of treatment. <a href="facial-cellulitis-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Facial cellulitis treatment</a> covers this in depth.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Facial Abscess</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">A walled collection of pus in the subcutaneous tissue. Presents as a well-defined, tender, fluid-filled swelling. Requires surgical drainage. <a href="facial-abscess-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Facial abscess treatment</a> has full details.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Space Infection</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Infection spreading into deep facial spaces — submasseteric, pterygomandibular, submandibular, or buccal spaces. Can cause trismus, difficulty swallowing, and airway risk. Requires IV antibiotics and possible drainage.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Necrotizing Fasciitis</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">A rare, rapidly destructive infection of the fascia and subcutaneous tissue. Produces disproportionate pain, skin discoloration, blistering, and systemic toxicity. A surgical emergency requiring aggressive debridement.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Erysipelas</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">A sharply demarcated streptococcal skin infection affecting the upper dermis and superficial lymphatics. Creates a raised, bright red, well-defined border on the face. Responds to penicillin-based antibiotics.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Orbital Cellulitis</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Infection spreading behind the eye — causes eye protrusion, pain with eye movement, double vision, and vision loss. An ophthalmological emergency requiring IV antibiotics and possible surgical drainage.</p></div>
</div>
