<li><h4 class="font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Incision and Drainage</h4><p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">For abscess collections — surgical drainage at CARE Hospitals operating rooms. May be performed under local or general anesthesia depending on location and depth.</p></li>
<li><h4 class="font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Surgical Debridement</h4><p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">For necrotizing fasciitis — aggressive surgical removal of all dead and infected tissue. May require multiple surgeries. Reconstructive surgery follows once the infection is controlled.</p></li>
</ul>
